    title: '2 Digit Divisor',
    ageBand: 'Primary (3-6)',
    developmentAreas: ['Mathematics'],
    subDevelopmentAreas: ['Decimal System: Dynamic: Stamp Game'],
    description: 'What is it?\n• The child takes out the stamps and writes a number for the dividend on the paper.\n• She chooses a divisor (from 1-99).\n• She places skittles for each hierarchy represented in the divisor (blue skittles for the tens and green skittles for the units).\n• Then she starts sharing out the dividend starting with the thousands, and writes each quantity down until she has a complete answer including hundreds, tens, and units.\nWhy do we do it?\n• See Stamp Game: Introduction\n• To practice long division\nHow to help at home?\n• Anytime it comes up that things at home have to be shared equally amongst people, allow your child to help.',
    mediaThumbUrl: 'https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/masterproject-a832a.appspot.com/o/amsCurriculum%2Flessons%2F18036627.png?alt=media&token=9ea731af-11dc-5abe-ad0a-4754b10f1312',
