    description: 'What is it?\n• Three boxes, differing only in color (red, blue, and yellow), each containing a set of graded figures as follows:\n- a set of 10 squares with increasing sides of length 1cm to 10cm\n- a set of 10 circles increasing in diameter from 1cm to 10cm\n- a set of 10 equilateral triangles with sides ranging from 1cm to 10cm.\n• This activity is an exploration of shape. The child can design anything with the shapes in the boxes.\nWhy do we do it?\n• To explore the relationships between and among geometric shapes.\nHow to help at home?\n• You can make these shapes at home out of paper.',
