    title: 'Grammar Symbols',
    ageBand: 'Primary (3-6)',
    developmentAreas: ['Language'],
    subDevelopmentAreas: ['Reading: Function of Words'],
    description: 'What is it?\n• The symbols used by the child to label the parts of speech while diagraming a sentence.\n• Small light blue triangle - definite and indefinite article\n• Medium dark blue triangle - Adjective\n• Large black triangle - Noun\n• Small pink rectangle - Conjunction\n• Small green crescent - Preposition\n• Large red circle - Verb\n• Small orange circle - Adverb\nWhy do we do it?\n• To help the child visualize the purpose of each word in a sentence.',
    mediaThumbUrl: 'https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/masterproject-a832a.appspot.com/o/amsCurriculum%2Flessons%2F18036558.jpeg?alt=media&token=6c9cd4a5-d597-54b7-a874-54cd40ba719b',
