    title: 'Window Washing',
    ageBand: 'Primary (3-6)',
    developmentAreas: ['Practical Life'],
    subDevelopmentAreas: ['Care of the Environment'],
    description: 'What is it?\n• The child uses a bucket and a chamois to clean the windows (or mirrors) in the classroom.\nWhy do we do it?\n• Coordination of movement of the whole body\n• Fine motor movements\n• Development of equilibrium\n• Development of order through exact use of each item and through following a logical sequence of actions\n• Motive for repetition, concentration, and exactness\n• Care of the environment',
    mediaThumbUrl: 'https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/masterproject-a832a.appspot.com/o/amsCurriculum%2Flessons%2F18036431.jpeg?alt=media&token=148c4915-5f5d-5610-a327-3c1711a0461a',
