    subDevelopmentAreas: ['Parts of Speech: The Verb'],
    description: 'What is it?\n• An exploration of active and passive verbs: the children recognize that the passive is formed by changing the form of the verb and moving the direct object to the subject: i.e. "Jane kicked the ball" becomes "The ball was kicked".\nWhy do we do it?\n• To open up avenues of discussion for writing style.\n• To realize that the subject of a verb is not always the agent (the main actor).\n• To enhance children\'s writing.\n• To aid in reading comprehension.\n• To draw attention to patterns in our language.\nSupporting interest at home:\n• See Parts of Speech.',
