    description: 'What is it?\n• A roll of black fabric representative of all time Earth has existed. The guide tells the story of the Earth, from its inception through the development of life. At the end of the strip is a piece of red fabric representative of the time which humans have existed.\n• Children are invited to hold the end and look back over the long black strip of Earth\'s story, compared with very short red strip of humanity\'s story.\nWhy do we do it?\n• To put the time humans have been on Earth in context.\n• To provide a visual representation of the comparative amount of time the Earth and humans have existed.\n• Repetition and elaboration of The Story of Creation/God Who Has No Hands, The Coming of Life, and the Timeline of Life.\nSupporting interest at home:\n• The show "Cosmos" may spark interest, and connects with many topics from the Montessori elementary lessons.',
