    title: 'Chart of Interdependencies',
    ageBand: 'Elementary (6-12)',
    developmentAreas: ['Biology'],
    subDevelopmentAreas: ['Chart of Interdependencies'],
    description: 'What is it?\n• This chart summarizes the interdependencies between the sun, the earth, plants, and animals.\n• It also presents the concept of "supranature", human culture that is built on top of the interdependencies of nature.\n• This work is presented when the children have done enough supporting work with geography, history and biology to be able to observe the connections between areas.\nWhy do we do it?\n• To help develop an understanding of the interrelationships that exist between all things.\n• To appreciate the fragile balance between all the things in the world.\n• To inspire a view of the world that is ecologically aware and sensitive, and to encourage a sense of responsibility toward the natural world.\nSupporting interest at home:\n• Seek opportunities with the child for them to learn and take action regarding the above mentioned interdependencies.',
    mediaThumbUrl: 'https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/masterproject-a832a.appspot.com/o/amsCurriculum%2Flessons%2F18035975.jpeg?alt=media&token=38fb17e4-6a87-5465-a9e2-4fd116ce6735',
