    ageBand: 'Elementary (6-12)',
    developmentAreas: ['Language'],
    subDevelopmentAreas: ['Parts of Speech: The Verb'],
    description: 'What is it?\n• The children act out different actions to experience the verb.\n• We show them a black pyramid and a red sphere to explain where our grammar symbols come from: nouns are solid and still, so we represent them with a black pyramid (flattened to a black triangle); verbs give a sentence energy, like a sphere that rolls around, so it is represented by a red circle.\nWhy do we do it?\n• To realize that verbs denote actions.\n• To build excitement about the function of words.\n• To give the experience of the function of the part of speech to the child.\nSupporting interest at home:\n• See Parts of Speech.',
